 "notes": "1917 cream-buff brick flats, four storeys. Ground (cream brick to 4.1 m): grilled laundromat shopfront left, recessed gated entry porch, a long blank painted-white brick wall with one high small window, a second shopfront right. Uppers: left bay, a wide central splayed bay carrying the steel fire escape, right-hand bay, paired small sash windows between, bracketed cornice. Cream trim. Rework r-eddy: red sign board over the shopfront at the left end. Storey count kept at 4: LiDAR 15.4 m with a 4.1 m ground leaves three 3.7 m uppers, a fifth storey does not fit. Tint lift (2026-10-02): paint tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k); brick tints converted to target / kit colour.",
